title: "Tidy Asset Allocation in R"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Stöckl"
    given-names: "Sebastian"
    affiliation: "University of Liechtenstein"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sstoeckl/tidy-asset-allocation"
url: "https://www.tidy-pm.com/dev/"
abstract: >-
  A course text on building, constraining and testing multi-asset portfolios
  with PortfolioAnalytics and the tidyverse: the question first, the
  mathematics in the running text, the method attributed to the literature,
  the code executed on a modeled multi-asset market that ships with the
  companion package tidypm, and takeaways and exercises at the end of every
  chapter.
keywords:
  - asset allocation
  - portfolio optimization
  - R
  - PortfolioAnalytics
  - textbook
